"The chamber is the Library's control center, beneath the main hall, and Links calls it a basement."
"The trunk is the Library's core, a petrified World Tree core that the Library's interface can reach."
"The blue veins in the core are ley lines of magic, not electricity; the Library uses no electricity."
"The alarm marks how little power is left, rather than an attack."
"Beneath the core, roots run to pools of power that hold only muddy dregs."
"A spiral staircase with no landings climbs two or three stories from the chamber to the main hall."
